<title>GERMANY: Experts more confident on EMU start - German poll.</title>
<headline>Experts more confident on EMU start - German poll.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A monthly survey by the German newspaper Handelsblatt has found experts in major banks and investment houses increasingly confident that Europe's single currency will be launched on time.</p>
<p>The chances of economic and monetary union (EMU) starting as planned in January 1999 were rated at an average of 75 percent by the experts in the poll, the paper said in an advance release from Thursday's edition.</p>
<p>The two percentage point increase from last month's figure was due in large part to moves by the new French government to cut its budget deficit, the paper said.</p>
</text>
